      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SANDFIRE ROSE (3) sets the standard after finishing within a length and a half of I'm Nipote in NMW1Y company at Ascot, and she now comes back from Saturday company into an easier assignment. Can find the front again here and will take plenty of catching with no weight on her back. POLYVANOVA (4) is the main danger. An eighth at Belmont reads plainly, but it was only just under four lengths in a CL3 and her Bunbury second before that was solid. Expecting a strong performance in what looks a suitable race. HERE FOR CHEQUES (2) drops out of mid-week NMW1Y grade and draws gate 1. LOOKS to get a lovely setup here and can play a leading role. SHOW ON THE ROAD (7) has been freshened, trialled at Lark Hill two weeks ago and gets weight relief after a plain Bunbury run, with his Northam third two back good enough to keep him in calculations. LOOKS (5) won't be far away.",
